Chapter 10: "The Lion King's Land"
Chapter 10-21: "The Six Tongues"

――An unprecedented calamity for the Kingdom of Lugunica, a crisis threatening national annihilation.

"――――"

Sitting up in bed, Subaru heard this and first pulled at his own cheek. It hurt. Meaning, this was definitely reality, not a continuation of a dream.

In other words――,

"Saying it's a continuation of a nightmare would almost be better than this endless string of 'what the hell.'... Am I, like, cursed or something? There's way too much shocking stuff going on..."

"In that case, it might not just be you who's cursed, Subaru. Chin up, I suppose."

"I can't feel the least bit chinned up, but thanks for being cursed together with me. I love you."

"And Betty too, I suppose."

Lowering the hand that had been pulling his cheek, Subaru used it to pat Beatrice's head instead. His reliable partner, who claimed to share his fate at the bedside, didn't seem to have received any more explanation about the current situation than Subaru had.

That being the case, he wanted to ask the people in this room who likely had more information――the 'White Sheep' and, this time for sure, Russell――a great many things, but...

"――'Shocking.' That was a word meaning surprised, or agitated, yes?"

"Huh? Ah, yeah, that's it... that's right, but why? Hardly anyone gets my hometown words on the first guess except Otto."

"No, it's nothing significant. It's just that recently, letters from Roswaal have frequently been mixed with such unfamiliar words. ...Since deciphering them is always a bit of extra work, I do wish he'd stop his pranks."

"You exchange letters with... Roswaal, I suppose?"

Beatrice narrowed her round eyes at Russell as he revealed why he'd reacted to the word Subaru had uttered, a slight hint of wariness rising in her. Normally, hearing the name of an ally should provide some measure of relief, but the fact that she couldn't accept it so easily really spoke to Roswaal's character.

Apparently thinking the same thing, Russell shrugged his shoulders with a "good grief," and said,

"It makes me uneasy, even as an outsider, to imagine how Roswaal interacts with Sir Natsuki and the rest of your camp. Allow me to defend myself by saying he is an old friend. We've known each other for about fifteen years now, I believe."

"Fifteen years...! That's a really long acquaintance. Wait, then could it be that when you lent us your strength for the White Whale subjugation..."

"Ah, as for that, please rest assured. Business and friendship are on entirely different lines. My decision to cooperate with Sir Natsuki at that time was my own; there was no room for Roswaal's intervention. In fact, had he asked me to, I might have refused?"

"Hmph. It seems you have a proper estimation of Roswaal, I suppose. If you'd said you were perfectly in sync best friends, I would have been ready to walk out right then and there, I suppose."

"The fact that badmouthing him earns him Beako's trust is so very Roswaal..."

That said, Russell's reply was welcome news from Subaru's perspective. The White Whale subjugation that Crusch and the others had planned――Subaru had voluntarily thought up and persuaded Anastasia and this very Russell to join as allies. If the negotiations that brought Russell on board had been set up by Roswaal, even with the same result, it would have slightly tarnished Subaru's self-assessment.

"U-Um, 'Silver Fox'... shouldn't we proceed with the discussion?"

The one who interjected there was the 'White Sheep,' left out of the conversation topic. She cast a concerned, upward glance at Russell, seemingly attempting to encourage the smooth progression of the talk, but her single remark introduced an unnecessary element of curiosity.

"――'Silver Fox,' huh. Can I take it you're willing to let me hear the details about that sort of thing?"

"Of course. Since we have welcomed Sir Natsuki in this way, we on our side must open our hearts and show an attitude of seeking your cooperation. However, before that..."

"...Before that?"

"I would like to confirm that Sir Natsuki is not a dangerous element. ――Yes, a 'check,' I believe they call it in your homeland."

Perhaps having learned that from Roswaal's letters as well, Russell stroked his neatly trimmed chin beard and deepened his smile as he looked at Subaru. Subaru's throat clicked unconsciously, a reaction to the sudden dryness he felt in his mouth. ――Mention of a dangerous element first brought to mind the 'Black Dog's' insinuation that Subaru was a Sin Archbishop. The humiliation of being lumped in with those wretches, who deserved every curse and insult the world had to offer.

But――,

"Russell-san, I don't know how I'm supposed to prove it, but that suspicion is wrong. The idea that I'm a Sin Archbishop or anything like that..."

"Words in defense are meaningless. That is the terror of the Witch's Cult. You should be well aware of this."

"――――"

"――Therefore, please take this."

At the unwavering, cold point, Subaru began to hang his head. Into his field of vision came something that Russell, who had walked closer from the room's entrance, suddenly held out.

His eyes fixed on it, Subaru caught his breath. There it was――,

"...My cellphone?"

A hoarse murmur escaped him as Subaru stared intently at the cellphone handed to him. There was no mistake, it was a mobile phone. Specifically, the flip phone Subaru himself had used and loved, an item he'd let go of long ago, one of the few things he'd brought from his original world.

He would never forget how he'd parted with it. It was the very object he had offered to Russell, right before his eyes, in exchange for his cooperation in the White Whale subjugation. ――Furthermore, he had cleverly rephrased its function, suggesting the phone had a sensor-like effect that warned of approaching demon beasts, in a way that didn't quite make it a lie.

"No, I mean, Russell-san... this is, how should I put it, not that there's no room for excuses, but there was no malice intended, I was forced by necessity, and if you ask whether it was bad or not, I'm incredibly, definitely in the wrong..."

"Wh-What's wrong, I suppose, Subaru? You're terribly flustered, I suppose."

"I never expected to run into the symbol of a sin I left behind in a place like this... B-But! Treating me like a Sin Archbishop for this sin is going way too far, I mean, unlike those guys, I'm fully prepared to apologize properly!"

"――No, that's quite alright. Confirmation achieved. You are indeed Sir Natsuki, without a doubt."

Sin Archbishops cannot apologize. ――No, there are those who superficially say "Thank you" or "I'm sorry," but none should be able to reflect from the heart and apologize.

So, Subaru, who had been about to deny the Sin Archbishop theory based on that reasoning, was instead unsettled by Russell's unexpected answer. "Eh?"

"Confirmation? All I did was hold my cellphone... Ah, was it because you knew the word 'cellphone'? That became proof of my innocence?"

"No, that's incorrect. Before it came into my possession, Sir Natsuki might have shown this off somewhere, spreading its name to any number of people; we cannot possibly grasp the extent of that. Therefore, rather than such external factors――I confirmed it with my own eyes."

"Your eyes... like a merchant's intuition?"

"That's not entirely wrong. It is a Divine Protection. It's called the 'Divine Protection of Appraisal,' you see; my eyes can discern the value of things I look at."

Pointing to his own eye and revealing his 'Divine Protection of Appraisal,' Russell directed that finger toward the cellphone in Subaru's hand. "And," he continued,

"That 'metia' only skyrockets in value while it's in your hands, Sir Natsuki."

"――!"

"Most likely, it is an object no one but Sir Natsuki can properly use. In my hands or anyone else's, that 'metia' emits no radiance whatsoever. However, while in your hands, it's different. Although, it has been silent for quite a long time now..."

"...Probably the battery's dead. But, it still shines in my hands?"

"Yes, dazzlingly so."

"I see. If it could be revived, it's because only I can do it..."

Savoring the incredibly nostalgic feel and weight in his hand, Subaru chewed over the words he'd been told and mulled over the logic Russell had used for his authentication. The cellphone was unusable by anyone but Subaru. Therefore, if it shone when in Subaru's hands, that was proof that he was the same existence now as he was back then――,

"...Wait? Does that mean, maybe, Russell-san, you knew from the start that you couldn't handle the cellphone yourself..."

"I became certain of it after you granted it to me as a reward. In my hands, or my subordinates', it held no value whatsoever. I thought that if the opportunity to question it ever arose, you would surely be quite surprised."

"Something like 'the one who got conned is at fault'... probably won't fly with Subaru, I suppose."

"It seems you understand well."

In a situation of equal negotiation, Subaru had, without lying, convinced Russell of the cellphone's value. That was something Crusch's 'Divine Protection of Wind Reading,' who had been present at that meeting, could attest to――but as Beatrice pointed out, Subaru feeling a sense of guilt was a different matter entirely.

Still, he never imagined that this unexpected reunion with his cellphone would vouch for his identity. He'd like to say that, but he couldn't claim this solved the problem.

"I hate to say this, but what that proved is just that I'm the same person now as I was during that negotiation. What if, before that, I was, I was... I was part of the Witch... the Witch's Cult..."

"Eep, even a hypothetical situation looks agonizingly painful!"

"That's how much his body and soul reject it, I suppose. I can understand the feeling, I suppose."

"Anyway! What if I was part of the Witch's Cult before that? And what's more, what if I was a Sin Archbishop?"

It was a supposition he hated to make himself, but complete innocence was desirable to clear suspicion. Even in the worst-case scenario, there was meaning in Subaru voicing it himself. Perhaps that could even be taken as a bit of credit material――,

"When you say 'before that'... that would be around the time the start of the Royal Selection was announced, yes?"

"Ah, yeah."

"Speaking of the start of the Royal Selection, I hear Sir Natsuki made quite the audacious declaration at the royal castle."

"Y-Yeah, that's right."

"I heard it earned him considerable animosity from many who were present, but fortunately, there were no outbursts from those around him, and as a result, it further lowered his reputation."

"R-Really...?"

"Would the Witch's Cult infiltrate by replacing Sir Natsuki in that state?"

"I guess not... The me back then would've been written off even by the Witch's Cult..."

Trying to appeal to human sympathy had only led to a merciless pile-on of logical truths, breaking Subaru's spirit. Indeed, any Witch's Cult that approached Subaru thinking he was exploitable after learning of his blunder at the castle was a fool, and if they had approached him beforehand, then Subaru blundering at the castle made him the fool. ――In other words, Subaru had proven his own innocence through the sheer foolishness of his actions.

"There's something I'm actually glad about from that event aside from my mental growth?!"

Furthermore, judging by the story just now, the mock battle with Julius after the blunder had apparently become null and void due to Julius's 'name' being eaten. In that case, the hate directed at Subaru from the kingdom knights was likely astronomical. Could it be that this was part of the reason he was now being pursued?

In any case――,

"So, from your perspective, Russell-san, I'm innocent?"

"Yes. From my perspective, it is no exaggeration to say that Sir Natsuki, considering your numerous exploits, is the individual I would most want to rely on in the current Kingdom of Lugunica."

"O-Oh, ohhh... I'm saved...! My heart is saved right now...!"

"Why are you so overcome with emotion by this man's words, I suppose! Betty, who believes in Subaru more than anyone, is right here by your side, I suppose! Emilia and the others too, I suppose!"

"Well, of course, that makes me so happy I could die, but there's a different depth of feeling between being trusted by your family and being trusted by an outsider. It's like the difference in difficulty level, you know?"

"Hmph. Betty is in a bad mood now, I suppose. The next time you're suspected of something, there'll be a five-minute penalty before Betty takes your side, I suppose."

"Five minutes where Beako isn't on my side...?! I wonder if I can endure that..."

Drawing the averted, puffed-cheek Beatrice onto the bed and settling her snugly into his crossed legs, Subaru said, "So," and looked at Russell again. Russell's side had finished their assessment of Subaru. That meant the next step was finally for Subaru's side to cut to the heart of the matter.

"It's about time you let me hear it. The story about the kingdom's trouble is important, but before that important talk, tell me about you and your group's true nature. You're not just an important merchant from the royal capital, are you?"

Of course, from what he'd heard so far, the category of 'capable merchant' could just barely cover it. However, Russell had said so at the very beginning. ――The kingdom faced an existential crisis, brought about by their sworn enemy of many years.

"An opponent who could potentially destroy a nation, and you call them a sworn enemy of many years – that doesn't sound like something a mere merchant would say. Same with them calling you 'Silver Fox,' Russell-san. You and that 'White Sheep' over there both have another real job. That is――"

"――'The Six Tongues.'"

"――!?"

Leaning forward eagerly, trying to get Russell to open his mouth, Subaru instead spun around in surprise at the voice from an unexpected direction. It was neither Russell nor the 'White Sheep' who had spoken. It was the person who, until now, had been silently listening to the conversation, apparently biding his time――,

"Rachins, how long have you been awake?"

"A while back. With this much chatter going on, how could I sleep forever? Though I almost yelped when Russell Fellow made his entrance, I'll admit."

The one who answered was Rachins, raising his body on the sofa. Seeing him wrapped in a blanket over his underclothes after his sewer-soiled garments had been removed, Subaru felt relief that he seemed safe for the moment.

"Setting aside the pretend-sleep eavesdropping... what did you just say? Six...?"

"'The Six Tongues,' I said. To put it plainly, it's an intelligence group that operates in the shadows of Lugunica... I never doubted they existed, but to think the head of the Merchant's Guild was their leader..."

"An intelligence group... you mean a spy organization?!"

The instant Rachins's explanation clicked in his head, Subaru couldn't help but raise his voice. Spies――that was a prime example of something that often appears in fiction but is rarely, if ever, encountered in nonfiction. Ninjas were close in category, but he had actually met real ones and even tasted their fearsomeness.

But could it really be that now――,

"In other words, your true identity is the shadow leader who runs the dark side of the Kingdom of Lugunica, Russell-san!"

Staring in astonishment, Subaru looked anew at Russell, who stood there with perfect posture. At Subaru's excessive reaction, Russell raised an eyebrow slightly, then slowly shook his head and said,

"Please don't go proclaiming that too loudly. ――It concerns your life, Sir Natsuki."

He delivered an answer that suggested, following the ninjas, he was about to taste the fearsomeness of spies as well.






