"Originally, the 'Six Tongues' were organized during the 'Demi-Human War' for the purpose of the kingdom's counter-intelligence activities. The prolonged civil war was partly due to underestimating the high intelligence-gathering capabilities of the demi-humans."

"Ah, that sounds likely. I have a friend who can mimic walls or the ground, after all."

"Yes. A specialized organization with knowledge of such traits, Divine Protections, or 'metia'... and the execution capability to handle them was needed. That is the reason the 'Six Tongues' was established, and I currently hold the position of its Director."

"Director...! That's the first time I've heard that title on this side...!"

"Why does Subaru get emotional over every single thing, I suppose? The suspiciousness of these people hasn't changed at all, I suppose. If anything, it's deepened, I suppose."

"Well, you're right. But in this case, the deeper the mystery, the more flavor it adds... that's what a secret intelligence agency is all about."

Pressing the cheek of the sulking Beatrice with his finger, Subaru glanced sidelong at Russell. Russell responded with the same unchanging posture and expression, but knowing his true identity as the head of an intelligence organization gave his presence and the pressure he exuded a new persuasive power.

Indeed, the history of the 'Six Tongues' founding made sense. ――The friend of Subaru's who could mimic things was Hyain of the Pleiades Battalion, and many demi-humans had participated in the war against the kingdom during the 'Demi-Human War.' And what proved useful in war wasn't just combat strength alone.

"By the way, Sir Rachins, where did you learn of the 'Six Tongues' existence? Was it from your father?"

"Huh? You think that old man would blab kingdom secrets just because we're family? It was just that I always figured something like that had to exist, and words I'd occasionally heard in rumors connected. I didn't have a speck of an idea that you were its representative, though."

"Is that so. As expected, Rickert Hoffman is a paragon of loyalty. Have you not been in contact with your father since then?"

"...Oi, your bad habits as an intelligence man are showing. Right now, it's your turn to talk, not the time for me to blab about this or that. Don't get carried away."

"You are absolutely right. My apologies."

To Rachins, whose glaring eyes sharpened further, Russell offered a theatrical bow. Even from that exchange, it seemed that the identity Rachins had revealed in the sewers――that his family was genuinely part of the kingdom's nobility――had been verified.

Receiving that response, Russell returned his gaze to Subaru. "Once again," he said,

"I cannot divulge details concerning classified matters, but our supreme goal is national defense. Including myself, all members conceal our positions, falsify our identities, and engage in counter-intelligence. The title of representative of the Royal Capital's Merchant's Guild also serves as a cover to hide the truth."

"As a cover, isn't it a bit too high-and-mighty? Being the Guild Master and all."

"It is the result of considering the necessary authority and influence for public appearances, as well as the balance. Rest assured, not every influential person in the Royal Capital is a member of the organization."

"――But now, it seems that situation might have been better, I suppose."

"Yes, to my shame, you are quite right about that."

Slowly shaking his head, Russell assumed a solemn expression at Beatrice's point. How much of that face reflected his true feelings was unknowable, but it seemed they were finally about to cut to the heart of the matter. The calamity currently assailing the Kingdom of Lugunica――it surely wasn't unrelated to the fact that Subaru's group had been cornered and that Emilia and the others had been targeted. And at the center of it was――

"――The 'Beloved Children.' That is currently the name of our... no, the kingdom's greatest enemy."

"Is it correct to say these guys are trying to destroy the Royal Selection?"

"That is not incorrect. However, it would be more accurate to say that what they are trying to destroy is not the Royal Selection, but the kingdom itself."

"The kingdom itself... and that impact is the current chaos in the Royal Capital? ...Come to think of it, you said earlier they were like a long-time enemy. What's that about?"

"Indeed. According to records... there are records of them operating in the shadows for over thirty years now."

"Thir...?!"

Having this completely unexpected number presented so matter-of-factly, Subaru's eyes widened in shock. He had imagined five or ten years, but not thirty. In the first place, if the 'Six Tongues' was an organization created after the 'Demi-Human War,' it should be about forty years since its founding.

"Thirty years from then... they've been fighting almost since it was made..."

"Yes. Therefore, the history of the 'Six Tongues' can also be called the history of a shadow war with the 'Beloved Children.' However, the 'Beloved Children' were an opponent whose true nature was unknown, and we were constantly on the back foot... We were barely managing to prevent them from running rampant within the country at will, a disgraceful state of affairs."

"Hah. For an organization sponsored by the kingdom, that's a pathetic story. Just taking a beating, huh."

"I have no words to return. In fact, throughout the kingdom, there are countless instances of feudal lords and influential figures suddenly changing their minds, or acts of treason passing information to other nations. For over a decade since I inherited the position of Director, we had no effective measures to break the deadlock, only continuing with symptomatic treatment. ――But the situation changed."

"Changed?"

"Yes. ――Because of the 'White Sheep' and the 'Black Dog.'"

Hearing this, Subaru silently looked at the 'White Sheep' standing by behind Russell. The 'Black Dog,' named alongside her, wasn't present here, but they had apparently helped the 'Six Tongues,' led by Russell, escape their dead end. As Subaru watched questioningly, wondering how on earth they had done it, the 'White Sheep' placed a hand on her chest, her lovely features tensing slightly.

"I was originally one of the 'Beloved Children.' And the 'Black Dog' shared the same circumstances."

"――! You mean you turned an enemy member?!"

"It was a situation aided by several coincidences. However, as a result, we were blessed with the opportunity to learn the secrets of the 'Beloved Children'... the enemy we had been opposing for so many years."

"Yes... Though, I didn't properly know everything myself, and there were things I could and couldn't speak of."

"No, even so, the gain is huge. That took a lot of resolve..."

The 'White Sheep' seemed somewhat diffident, but that likely diverged from Russell's assessment. After all, as the key person who had moved a battle stagnant for thirty years, the 'Six Tongues' must have felt an emotion akin to finding an oasis in the desert. At Subaru's impression, the 'White Sheep' lowered her gaze slightly.

"...You're right. I surprised even myself. That I had such courage. ...If that's the case, then sooner..."

"――?"

"Ah, no, it's nothing! Anyway, that's my position in all this!"

Subaru furrowed his brow slightly at the 'White Sheep' waving her hands frantically, and held his tongue. But before he could press that point of curiosity, Rachins's rough voice snapped, "Oi."

"Can we really trust a story about betrayal? For all I know, this enemy you bastards are tired of might be a trap they sent in to manipulate you as they please, yeah?"

"In that case, it would be more natural for us to have been crushed long ago. It has already been over a year since the 'White Sheep' and others joined our side... During that time, the 'Beloved Children's' covert activities they've thwarted are too many to count on one hand. There would be no point in contributing this much otherwise."

"...There might be a point. I'm saying the vigilance is lacking."

"――Please do not worry. Measures to prevent their betrayal have been taken. It is by those measures that they bought my trust... no, earned it."

With sharp gazes, Rachins and Russell faced each other, exchanging opinions. Subaru could understand Rachins's point, but he had a strong independent impression of Russell as someone shrewd. With Rachins, the first impression of him from his back-alley thug days just wouldn't go away, so there was a clear difference in the caliber of the actors.

"...Is it heartless of me to think that, after being helped by him?"

"If we're just talking about the number of times, being protected here is thanks to Whiskers, I suppose. Even counting being saved in the sewers, it's even between the thug and Whiskers, I suppose."

"True. As expected, my Beako can do math――"

"――Um, Natsuki Subaru-san."

Swaying together with Beatrice nestled in his crossed legs, Subaru had been wavering over which side to favor when the 'White Sheep's' call made him respond with a strange "Nyah?" But she looked at Subaru earnestly, then bowed her head deeply. And then――

"The reason we were able to escape from the 'Beloved Children'... is thanks to all of you. So, I've wanted to thank you for so long... Thank you very much."

"Huh? You're welcome, but for what specifically is this gratitude?"

"Of course, for the subjugation of the Witch Cult's Sin Archbishop of 'Sloth'!"

"...Petelgeuse?"

Subaru blinked and asked back, and the 'White Sheep' nodded vigorously with a "Yes!" Between the incident at the royal castle, that symbol of his dark past, and the matter of the White Whale subjugation involving his cellphone, this was a day where events from the very start of the Royal Selection were being dug up excessively. But while he could understand being praised for defeating Petelgeuse Romanée-Conti, he didn't understand the reason for such direct thanks from the 'White Sheep.'

"Don't tell me you were one of that bastard's 'Fingers' or something?"

"Fin...? No, that's wrong, but... it caused a huge uproar for Mama, and we took advantage of that chaos to..."

"Huh? Huh? Huh? Wait, wait, I'm getting lost again. A Mama who was thrown into chaos by Petelgeuse's disappearance? Just what was this chaos..."

"――I didn't know her true identity for the longest time either. She always looked different when we met, and I never got to have a proper conversation... But I finally understood."

Though Subaru expressed his confusion, the 'White Sheep,' speaking with excitement, also seemed unable to control her surging emotions. She wasn't answering Subaru's question but rather, as if opening the lid on a secret she had long held inside, her eyes glistened.

"The one I... the one we, the 'Beloved Children,' were made to follow all along... that is――"

"W-Wait, my emotions haven't caught up yet..."

"――Capella Emerada Lugunica."

"――Ah?"

Suddenly, the ominous sound striking his eardrums made his bewildered thoughts freeze over in an instant. The multitude of unprocessed information and emotions fell silent as if doused with water, and Subaru, breathless, stared intently at the 'White Sheep.' She nodded back at his gaze, moved her thin lips once more, and said clearly:

"――The Sin Archbishop of 'Lust,' Capella Emerada Lugunica. That is the wicked person who made us 'Beloved Children' call her Mama and obey her!"

"――. ――――. ――――――――. You're kidding."

It took a considerable amount of time to accept and process the name that the 'White Sheep' had spoken. Breaking it down, chewing it over, swallowing it, ruminating on it again, repeating the process.

"――――"

As Subaru fell silent, Russell called out, "'White Sheep.'" He infused his voice with a slightly reproachful nuance.

"I intended to explain this in a proper sequence. Bringing up that name was somewhat hasty."

"Ah, I-I'm sorry! I... got ahead of myself..."

"I did intend to speak of it, but handle information with care. A card in hand is like your life. I should have taught you this many times over this past year."

"Y-Yes..."

Deflated, the 'White Sheep' cast her eyes down at Russell's words. However, while Subaru felt sorry for the dejected 'White Sheep,' the time taken for that scolding allowed his mind, which had stopped working from the shock, to start moving again.

――The Sin Archbishop of 'Lust,' Capella Emerada Lugunica.

Every Sin Archbishop of the Witch's Cult could be summed up in a single word: the worst. But the evil of Capella's nature was an object of Subaru's particular loathing, even compared to the other Archbishops. He had only encountered her once, during the battle at the city hall of the Watergate City of Priestella, but honestly, she was the prime example of someone he never wanted to meet again if he could help it. To hear Capella's name here, of all times...

"Mama, and the 'Beloved Children'..."

"When they're lined up together, it's a combination of words that makes you feel sick, I suppose."

"Plus, I can totally imagine her saying that. ...No wonder 'White Sheep'-chan wanted to run away."

Subaru wrinkled his brow and twisted his lips, and Beatrice turned a concerned eye toward him. Fortunately, Beatrice hadn't seen the real Capella, and Subaru thought that was for the best. All Sin Archbishops were bad for Beatrice's emotional development. Capella especially so, he wanted to add.

"Mama... Capella gathers various children from various places and treats them all as her own children. She tells you to think of her as your mother. But..."

"Evil, dangerous, moral harassment... I can imagine it all. ...Can't shake the habit?"

"It's quite difficult... We've all had it ingrained into our bodies."

With a smile too painful to call a wry one, the 'White Sheep' spoke of her past. The fact that even after defecting from the 'Beloved Children' and escaping Capella's control, she still called the object of her terror 'Mama' was proof of the magnitude of the harsh circumstances she had endured. And if Subaru's group defeating Petelgeuse had helped her escape that hellish situation――

"I'm glad. That 'White Sheep'-chan got out."

"Natsuki Subaru-san..."

"Ah, but, I think that 'Black Dog' one isn't grateful enough. That guy seemed ready to scorch me and my adorable Beako whole. Trying to return a favor with a grudge. I won't forgive him unless he apologizes."

"Won't forgive him, I suppose."

Matching Subaru's sharply pointed finger, Beatrice pointed at the 'White Sheep' with the same motion. Looking at the two fingers thrust toward her and the simultaneous wink from Subaru and Beatrice, the 'White Sheep' blinked in surprise, then laughed quietly.

"Yes... I understand. I will definitely make the 'Black Dog' apologize."

"Please do. So, the opponent is Capella... Are the 'Beloved Children' like a troop name within the Witch's Cult? Like Petelgeuse's 'Fingers' or Regulus's 'Wives'..."

"If she heard you call it that, Sylphy would beat you up, I suppose. Don't say such careless things, I suppose. Subaru isn't exactly in Sylphy's good graces as it is, I suppose."

"I contributed quite a bit to defeating Regulus too, though... Well, I welcome more girls who support Emilia-tan, so we'll have to bond over being her fans someday."

Sylphy, one of the members currently on standby at the Roswaal mansion, was a woman who had originally been one of Regulus's wives but was now a staunch supporter of Emilia. Thinking about it, with Subaru being pursued and even Emilia captured, the camp was in dire straits. That made him worry about those left behind at the mansion: Sylphy, Ryuzu, and the replica Ryuzu, Meili. Regarding that, he had no choice but to pin his hopes on the personnel who could act outside the Royal Capital――Roswaal.

"Worrying about that aside... What's your take, 'White Sheep'-chan?"

"...At the very least, I never had that perception of myself. I've never even met a Witch Cultist."

"I-Is that so... So, a separate unit from the Witch Cultists, or more like a private army for each Sin Archbishop? Either way, calling them 'Beloved Children' is a disgustingly nasty way to put it."

It wasn't quite 'hate the priest, hate the robe,' but when Subaru thought of Capella's involvement, his feelings made him want to find fault with everything.

"――――"

Reflexively, Subaru glanced toward Crusch, sleeping on the adjacent bed. Putting aside his own arms and legs, the 'Dragon's Blood' poured into Crusch's body was also a scar left by Capella. Many people in Priestella had their forms changed by that woman's hand and remained sleeping in ice. ――Just like 'Gluttony,' 'Lust' destroyed too many people's lives.

"Besides, it makes sense that you guys couldn't catch their tail for thirty years. That person can change her appearance however she pleases. That's why..."

"She was never accurately identified before. That came to light only after the information about the Sin Archbishop of 'Lust,' who exposed her true form and wielded her Authority in Priestella, matched the profile of the entity known to the 'White Sheep' and the others."

"Conspiring in the shadows, doing whatever she wanted, huh..."

"Yes. The abrupt changes of heart and treasonous acts by the feudal lords and influential figures are, in fact, no mystery. ――They had all, likely, been replaced."

"That's someone who could do something like that. Truly the worst――"

As Subaru nodded at Russell's conjecture and was about to spit out his disgust at its maliciousness, he realized something. If that conjecture were to develop further, it would mean acknowledging something incredibly terrifying. And that was, unmistakably――a quiet, thorough invasion, a crisis threatening the kingdom's very existence.

"Oi, oi, oi, you can't mean..."

"――It's the worst, I suppose."

As if arriving at the same thought Subaru had perceived at the same moment, Rachins, his face rigid, trembled as his voice failed to put the looming possibility into words. Beatrice also shrank her shoulders within Subaru's crossed legs and shuddered.

"Russell-san..."

"Yes. The three of you have imagined correctly. Hence, the kingdom's greatest peril."

Though afraid to hear the answer, Subaru had no choice but to ask. Russell, who had already finished his own battle with the shock and advanced to the next stage, nodded deeply. And then, the Director of the 'Six Tongues,' the man entrusted with the mission of protecting the kingdom, declared:

"The kingdom's 'Council of Elders,' along with the majority of its high-ranking nobles, have been replaced by Capella Emerada Lugunica, who leads the 'Beloved Children,' and there is a high probability that the Dragon Tablet is in the hands of this 'Lust.'"








